<!--
     FALLBACK ONLY. Once the blog has been published even once, _worker.js
     serves a generated sitemap out of KV instead of this file. It has to:
     posts appear and disappear without a redeploy, and a static file can't
     track them. This copy is what gets served before that first publish.
     See render_sitemap_xml() in app/modules/blog.py.

     terms-of-service.html, privacy-policy.html and cookie-policy.html are
     all left out on purpose. They carry a noindex robots meta tag (legal
     boilerplate, not content anyone should reach from a search result),
     and listing noindex pages in a sitemap is a known anti-pattern that
     just produces "Submitted URL marked noindex" warnings in Search
     Console.

     /blog/ is absent for the same reason while the blog is empty: that
     address currently serves landing/blog/index.html, a noindex
     placeholder. The generated sitemap that replaces this file at first
     publish does include /blog/, because by then it is a real listing.

     CAREFUL: a double hyphen is not legal inside an XML comment. Two of
     them in this file's previous version made the whole sitemap
     unparseable, and Google reported it as "1 error, 0 discovered pages"
     with no indication of the cause. Use commas or full stops instead of
     dashes when editing this header.

     Part A1 (EN/ES dual language): /es/ and /es/security.html are the
     Spanish homepage/security page, routed by _worker.js to
     index.es.html/security.es.html. Same noindex exclusion rule as
     above keeps the Spanish legal pages (which carry the identical
     noindex meta tag as their English originals) out of this list too.
-->
